{
  "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/education",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "en": "education"
  },
  "definition": {
    "en": "An intentional process that supports learning and the development of knowledge, understanding, skills, competences, attitudes and values through communication and organised activities."
  },
  "scopeNote": {
    "en": [
      "For statistical purposes, UNESCO’s International Standard Classification of Education (ISCED 2011) provides an operational framework for classifying education programmes and qualifications across countries. It covers formal and non-formal education throughout life. Informal learning is excluded from measures of participation in education, although recognised qualifications obtained through it may count towards educational attainment. Beyond its statistical meaning, education is recognised as a fundamental human right. UNESCO’s Rethinking Education: Towards a Global Common Good? (2015) proposes understanding education as a common good, emphasising its individual and collective purposes. These perspectives address complementary questions: how education is classified and measured, and what purposes it should serve."
    ]
  },
  "notation": [
    "5.3"
  ],
